    rt_interp_cstr_built_name_unterminated_runtime_path_2026-11-26, fixing, p3sweep2-20261127, 2026-11-27T18:01:43Z, 2026-11-27T18:01:43Z, open, "wave8"

    rt_interp_cstr_built_name_unterminated_runtime_path_2026-11-26, 0, "2026-11-27 p3sweep2-61127: reproduced deterministically (20/20 runs) on the seed lane: JIT fixture with extern fn rt_interp_cstr + strlen printed len=34 strlen=46 - 12 bytes of heap slack over-read. Root cause: src/compiler_rust/runtime/src/value/collections.rs:4448 rt_interp_cstr returned rt_string_data(value) verbatim; alloc_runtime_string (collections.rs:893) allocates exactly sizeof(RuntimeString)+len with NO trailing NUL, so every C-string consumer (rt_cuda_module_get_function, dlopen/dlsym twins, collection capture, spawn facades in mixed links) over-reads whenever the Rust definition wins the link (the C twin returns a terminated buffer). Fix (doc option 2, terminated copy, no layout change): INTERP_CSTR_BUFFER RefCell<Vec<u8>> added to the existing thread_local block (TRANSIENT_HEAP_SCOPE idiom); rt_interp_cstr copies bytes into the per-thread buffer and appends NUL; raw-pointer passthrough unchanged; doc comment records the borrowed contract (valid until the next same-thread call - every consumer reads immediately, verified call-by-call); interp_cstr_tests updated (it asserted the buggy pointer identity). Spec test/02_integration/compiler/backend/interp_cstr_termination_abi_spec.spl (new, SIMPLE_BINARY-overridable, recipe in header): RED on unpatched fresh-seed AND on an unpatched baseline scratch build, GREEN on the patched scratch (1 passed); cargo test -p simple-runtime --lib value::collections 271 passed 0 failed incl the new returns_nul_terminated_copy_for_runtime_string. No C runtime touched; no new warnings. Residual: capture_begin_note_finish_round_trip in simple-compiler fails identically on unpatched HEAD (another lane's concurrent edits, not this fix); on platforms with zeroed heap slack the RED would be vacuous while GREEN stays valid (evidence contract documented in the spec header). close_evidence reproducer=test/02_integration/compiler/backend/interp_cstr_termination_abi_spec.spl prevention=test/fixtures/compiler/interp_cstr_termination/main.spl"
